{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I will utterly gather</b> — The alef of אסוף is a sign of the future of the nifal binyan, from the root of ספו תמו. The meaning is the future binyan." "<b>Gather</b> — Every verb properly has three root letters, and when the verb comes in the pa'el [pi'el] form — הכביד, האביד, השמיד — it is called the doubled [nifal/nifal-type] binyan. And some say: the alef of אסוף is added, like the alef of אדוש ידושנו."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The reference to 'the doubled binyan' is hyper-literal for 'הנוסף' in the parallel comment [0]; I retain his terminology exactly. The pi'el examples are his own Hebrew forms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:14.875777587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}